 ## Operating characteristics
 - **Time Complexity:** The predictor is of the highest possible order among all predictors attempting to predict the value at one corner of a cube from the other $2^n - 1$ corners [S1, unofficial]. The computational cost per sample is $O(2^n)$ for the prediction sum [S1, unofficial].
-- **Memory Complexity:** The memory footprint is small, proportional to the size of one slice plus lower-dimensional footprints. In $R^4$, the buffer size is $X_M Y_M Z_M + X_M Y_M + X_M + 1$ [S1, unofficial]. This makes it well-suited for out-of-core implementations [S1, unofficial].
+- **Memory Complexity:** The memory footprint is small, proportional to the size of one slice plus lower-dimensional footprints [S1, unofficial]. In $R^4$, the buffer size is $X_M Y_M Z_M + X_M Y_M + X_M + 1$ [S1, unofficial]. This makes it well-suited for out-of-core implementations [S1, unofficial].
 - **Measured Performance:**
   - On a 3D model of a house on fire (43,202,395 bytes uncompressed), 4D Lorenzo compression reduced the size to 524,768 bytes (1.21% of total), outperforming 3D slice compression (1,076,587 bytes, 2.49%) by 50% [S1, unofficial].
